{title: Porch Light}
{artist: Fretbook Demo}
{comment: An original song written for Fretbook (CC0). Four easy chords: strum down, down-up, up-down-up.}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[C]Porch light's on and the [G]kettle's low
[Am]Nowhere left that we [F]need to go
[C]Dust in the window, a [G]slow guitar
[Am]Home is just wherever [F]we are
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Leave the light on, [C]leave the door
[G]Play it once and [Am]play it more
[F]Leave the light on, [C]stay a while
[G]Every chord is [C]worth a smile
{end_of_chorus}
